From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simone Primarosa <simone.primarosa@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +01:00
Subject: [PATCH] feat: implement partial worker stop for raycluster and rayjob workloads

Preemption of Ray workloads in Kueue is entirely all-or-nothing, terminating the Ray Head pod, distributed state, and active drivers even when preempting only a subset of worker pods would free sufficient quota. Restarting the head pod destroys long-running checkpoints and driver connections, whereas elastic Ray clusters can dynamically shrink worker groups without interrupting head execution.

Implement collaborative partial worker stopping for RayCluster and RayJob workloads by exposing the kueue.x-k8s.io/reclaim-target-counts annotation and reconciling partial preemption requests. Stop surplus worker pods in whole replica units by deletion cost and age while keeping the Ray Head pod and core cluster state operational. For a RayCluster, and for a RayJob with in-tree autoscaling, lower each shrunk worker group to its target and list the stopped pods in its scaleStrategy.workersToDelete, so KubeRay removes exactly those pods instead of recreating them and the Ray autoscaler starts from the lower replicas, once per reclaim request, which a Workload annotation records.
